date:     2026-09-25
time:     14:30:00
datetime: 2026-09-25T14:30:00
decimal:  123.45

-- a decimal is exact; a double is not --
0.1D + 0.2D = 0.3
0.1  + 0.2  = 0.30000000000000004
1D / 3D     = 0.33333333333333333333333333333333333333
19.99D * 3D = 59.97

-- a hundred pennies is a pound, which in DOUBLE it is not --
decimal: 1  equal to 1? 1
double:  1.0000000000000007  equal to 1? 0

-- converting from text, which is how these arrive --
2026-01-02 09:05:00 2026-01-02T09:05:00
CDEC of 0.1 plus 0.2 = 0.3
a DATETIME gives either half: 2026-01-02 09:05:00

-- comparison is by value, not by text --
later date?   1
same instant? 1
exact money?  1

-- text still assigns, as it does from a file --
2026-03-04
and STR$ of one is what PRINT shows: 123.45

-- # has meant a file number since the 1970s, and still does --
written through a file number
